INT. HOLLOW GIANT OAK - TWILIGHT

A throne room carved inside a dead tree. Roots for pillars. Fireflies in jars.

QUEEN ELSPETH, 70s, sits wrapped in moss-green wool. Her crown is a ring of antlers. A cloaked FIGURE stands in the doorway, dripping. Beside the throne, SIR BRAM THORNWICK, 50s, one-armed knight, rests a hand on his hilt. Two PAGES, TWIG and NETTLE, twins, 10, hide behind a root.

STRANGER
I came about the debt.

QUEEN ELSPETH
Debts are paid at dawn. This is dusk.

STRANGER
Then I'm early.

Bram steps forward. Sword half drawn.

SIR BRAM
Name yourself.

The Stranger lowers the hood. A woman, 30s, bark-pale skin, eyes like polished amber.

STRANGER
You know it. Say it, Brammy.

Bram releases the sword. Stares.

SIR BRAM
Wrenna.

WRENNA
Wrenna Ashgrove. The tree-keeper's daughter. The one you left under the roots.

QUEEN ELSPETH
You were dead.

WRENNA
So were the roots, once.

Twig whispers to Nettle. Nettle shushes her.

TWIG
(whispering)
Is she a ghost?

NETTLE
Ghosts don't drip.

Wrenna sets a small acorn on the floor. It cracks. A green shoot unfurls, and stops. Wilts. She sighs.

WRENNA
I thought I'd have more left.

QUEEN ELSPETH
Sit, child.

Wrenna sits on a root. Elspeth sets her crown aside.

QUEEN ELSPETH (CONT'D)
The debt is forgiven.

WRENNA
I didn't come to be forgiven.

SIR BRAM
Then what?

WRENNA
To see it. Once. Before it falls.

The fireflies dim, one jar at a time.
